# Adobe's Core-14 AFM files and their licence are vendored BYTE-EXACT under APAFML, which requires
# that any modification be prominently noted in the modified file and that the licence paragraph
# itself not be modified. Line-ending normalisation is a modification: `MustRead.html` carries the
# original classic-Mac CR endings and the .afm files carry CRLF, and a checkout that rewrote either
# would break the pinned sha256 digests in vendor/afm/README.md and the obligation with them.
#
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion on these paths, whatever the client's core.autocrlf.
vendor/afm/** -text

# Shell scripts run under Git Bash on the Windows release runner, and bash reads a CRLF line's `\r`
# as part of the command. `eol=lf` fixes the checkout ending whatever core.autocrlf a client set,
# so `ci/*.sh` arrives runnable on every clone. `fixtures/gate` needs no line here: git classifies
# all eight PDFs as binary (`git ls-files --eol`), and autocrlf converts only what it takes for text.
*.sh text eol=lf
